%[text] # Explore NASA Flight Data
%[text] This live script uses the functions included in the **`AirSpeedVirtualSensor`** package to load flight data, clean sensor readings, explore the data, and fit a virtual airspeed sensor.
%[text:tableOfContents]{"heading":"Contents"}
%%
%[text] ## Package Functions
%[text] The package includes these main functions:
%[text] - **`loadFlightData`** imports the aircraft sensor workbook.
%[text] - **`cleanFlightData`** removes ground samples and repairs oil sensor dropouts.
%[text] - **`sampleFlightRows`** selects rows for responsive plots.
%[text] - **`renderExplorePlot`** creates the prediction-check plot used by the app.
%[text] - **`fitVirtualSensor`** fits the true-airspeed model. \
%%
%[text] ## Load and Clean Flight Data
%[text] Load the NASA aircraft sensor data, then clean it for flight analysis.
rawData = loadFlightData("FlightData.xlsx");
[flightData, cleaningSummary] = cleanFlightData(rawData);
head(flightData) %[output:7b32a495]
struct2table(cleaningSummary) %[output:48c766ee]
%%
%[text] ## Explore a Flight Trend
%[text] View true airspeed across the flight with a gradient line chart.
trendRows = sampleFlightRows(height(flightData), 3000);
trendWindow = uifigure(Name="True airspeed trend", Position=[120 120 820 460]); %[output:23ca7c8e]
trendChart = LineGradientChart(Parent=trendWindow, ... %[output:23ca7c8e]
    XData=flightData.Time(trendRows), ... %[output:23ca7c8e]
    YData=flightData.TrueAirSpeed(trendRows), ... %[output:23ca7c8e]
    LineWidth=4); %[output:23ca7c8e]
colormap(trendChart, turbo(256)) %[output:23ca7c8e]
trendColorbar = colorbar(trendChart); %[output:23ca7c8e]
trendColorbar.Label.String = "True airspeed (knots)"; %[output:23ca7c8e]
title(trendChart, "True airspeed across the flight") %[output:23ca7c8e]
xlabel(trendChart, "Time") %[output:23ca7c8e]
ylabel(trendChart, "True airspeed (knots)") %[output:23ca7c8e]
%%
%[text] ## Compare a Predictor
%[text] Screen fan speed against true airspeed with a fitted relationship.
rows = sampleFlightRows(height(flightData), 2500);
x = flightData.FanSpeed(rows);
y = flightData.TrueAirSpeed(rows);
validRows = isfinite(x) & isfinite(y);
relationshipWindow = uifigure(Name="Fan speed relationship", Position=[140 140 760 430]); %[output:66a76dd7]
relationshipChart = ScatterFitChart(Parent=relationshipWindow, ... %[output:66a76dd7]
    XData=x(validRows), ... %[output:66a76dd7]
    YData=y(validRows), ... %[output:66a76dd7]
    SizeData=30, ... %[output:66a76dd7]
    Marker="o", ... %[output:66a76dd7]
    LineWidth=2.4, ... %[output:66a76dd7]
    Controls="off"); %[output:66a76dd7]
legend(relationshipChart, "off") %[output:66a76dd7]
grid(relationshipChart, "on") %[output:66a76dd7]
title(relationshipChart, "Fan speed vs. true airspeed") %[output:66a76dd7]
xlabel(relationshipChart, "Fan speed (rpm)") %[output:66a76dd7]
ylabel(relationshipChart, "True airspeed (knots)") %[output:66a76dd7]
%%
%[text] ## Fit the Virtual Sensor
%[text] Fit the model, then compare predicted and measured airspeed on the test data.
model = fitVirtualSensor(flightData);
flightData.PredictedTrueAirSpeed = model.PredictedTrueAirSpeed;
predictionWindow = uifigure(Name="Virtual sensor prediction check", Position=[160 160 820 460]); %[output:0ec90cfe]
predictionAxes = uiaxes(predictionWindow, Position=[50 50 720 350]); %[output:0ec90cfe]
renderExplorePlot(predictionAxes, flightData, "Prediction check", ... %[output:0ec90cfe]
    "PredictedTrueAirSpeed", "TrueAirSpeed"); %[output:0ec90cfe]
title(predictionAxes, "Virtual sensor prediction check") %[output:0ec90cfe]
legend(predictionAxes, ["Measured", "Predicted"], ... %[output:group:3c66fd0f] %[output:0ec90cfe]
    Location="southoutside", Orientation="horizontal") %[output:group:3c66fd0f] %[output:0ec90cfe]
%%
%[text] ## Results
%[text] The package functions support the complete workflow: import sensor data, prepare it for analysis, explore relationships, and estimate true airspeed from the available signals.

